From 827da2340003905af67faeaa652cb725b624f737 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:41:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-8 first five data planes

Implement the first five batch-8 Unit data planes on top of the reconciled
canonical chain. Base in the reconciled canonical order is the 26-layer chain
through 0145 (canonical 75f1d24 plus 0120-0129, 0131, 0134, 0136, 0130, 0133,
0135, 0132, 0137, 0138, 0139, 0140, 0141, 0142, 0143, 0144 and 0145); this is
the 27th layer after 0120 and it applies at the chain end. No guest/Device
Service evidence is recorded; all five stay planned and the reused register
machines keep their existing NOT RUN boundaries.

- pahub-v21 (U040-B-V21): reuses the PCA9548A mask-only PaHub model and adds a
  0x70-0x77 DIP-address fixture; downstream bus forwarding/nested hubs are
  NOT modeled and 0x70-0x77 conflicts with pahub/pahub-v20/env-iii.
- gps-v11 (U032-V11) / gps-sma (U190): reuse the batch-4 GPS UART NMEA
  injection path for AT6668 with a baud fixture (default 9600) that keeps the
  product page 115200 vs frozen driver 9600 conflict UNRESOLVED; GNSS RF/
  antenna/constellation/accuracy are NOT RUN and PORT.C is shared with UART
  Units.
- lcd (U120): new CONTROL_UNIT_LCD ST7789V2 I2C command/framebuffer slave
  (READ_ID 0x04, READ_BUFCOUNT 0x09, FILLRECT 0x68-0x6C, CASET 0x2A/RASET
  0x2B, WRITE_RAW 0x41-0x44, WRITE_RLE 0x49-0x4D, DRAWPIXEL, SET_COLOR,
  BRIGHTNESS/ROTATE/POWER/SLEEP, CHANGE_ADDR 0xA0) with a 135x240 RGB565
  framebuffer and bufcount; the page 0x3E vs frozen driver 0x3D address
  conflict is UNRESOLVED (driver address used, CHANGE_ADDR applies) and
  display composition/optics/backlight/ESP32-PICO firmware are NOT RUN.
- mini-can (U179): the CAN Unit attachment/TWAI frame injection path is not
  modeled in this Unit runtime (same gap as batch7 can), so the catalog/profile
  entry stays planned/blocked; TJA1051 electrical/termination/arbitration
  behavior are NOT RUN. (The batch-7 0145 layer binds the cores3 CAN model for
  the `can`/`mini-can` ids; this batch-8 layer does not add a second path.)

Offline QOM smoke (S3 m5atoms3r, no guest firmware): the pahub-v21/lcd/
gps-v11/gps-sma attachments check property registration, fixtures, the pahub
DIP address move and the LCD read-id/bufcount: 20/20 PASS. The smoke is not a
functional PASS and I2C command bytes/guest NMEA decode/CAN frames still need
guest evidence.
---
